From: FE Fates port <port@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:02:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/21] core: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: files patched in
 the read get an in-place LZ13 size

The game decompresses an LZ13 file in place: the stored bytes sit at the end of a
buffer of the LZ13 outer size and are read forward while the output is written from
the buffer's start. The game's own outer size is exactly what that needs: for every
one of the 302 chapter person and placement files of the clean dump, outer = stored
size + the largest (bytes written - next byte read) over the stream.

A file patched in the read is compressed by our own parse and zero padded to the
original size, but kept the original outer size, so the writes ran over the unread
end of the stream. The end of the file is its string pool: in the round 59 smoke a
song name written into a Seal of Flames chapter person file (S002) read back as other
bytes, while every cell before the pool was right. Round 58's wrong placement labels
(Birthright 4: two joiners with no weapon; patch 0015 sends those files to the
in-memory path) are the same fault: labels live in the pool.

patch_stored now writes the outer size this stream needs (`inplace_margin`), never
less than the original or the data size. Checked: `cargo test -p zakuro-core --lib`
181 passed (new patched_lz13_decodes_in_place decodes in place as the game does).
